We finish eating and go to the living room.
Deepa brings warm jeera water.
I open the halwa box.
"We can eat this sweet now," I say.
Deepa takes a piece of halwa.
"This is very tasty," Deepa says.
Outside, heavy rain is falling.
We talk about our families.
Deepa asks about Mexico.
"My family is in Mexico," I say.
"I will come to Mexico one day," Deepa says.
"I think that Kochi is a beautiful place," I say.
Deepa smiles happily.
Now, we are not just colleagues.
I think that we are good friends.
